  "body": "## What changed\n\nA probe-only program posted with \"stock sim did not judge this program: invalid stock simulation setup: stock box and cell must be finite, box non-empty, cell positive\". That names the wrong cause; the stock was fine.\n\n**Cause:**\n- A touch probe stays out of the program sim's plan, because it removes nothing (#108). In a probe-only program the plan is therefore empty.\n- The stock lattice is sized by `min(radius)` over the planned tools, which is +inf over an empty plan.\n- The infinite cell was then refused as an invalid setup.\n\n**Fix (`crates/app/src/stock_sim.rs`, `stock_grid`):** when no tool radius is finite, the lattice is sized by the stock's span alone (`auto_cell(0, span)`, the grid ceiling's floor).\n- **What the sim does now:** it judges the uncut stock against the part. That reads clean when they agree and rest where they differ, and it cannot report a gouge it never cut.\n- **Unchanged:** a missing or invalid stock still refuses by its own name, and `auto_cell` in the sim crate is untouched.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/592-probe-only-sim.md`. It records why I judged the uncut stock rather than skipping the sim with a note.\n\n## How tested\n\n- **New `crates/app/tests/probe_only_sim.rs`, 2/2:**\n  - `a_probe_only_program_is_judged_not_refused_as_an_invalid_setup`: a 3 × 2 × 1 in part with stock equal to it, and one top-face probe. `verification_report` has no problems and **no not-judged note**. It **fails without the fix**, with the old note present.\n  - `a_probe_only_program_without_a_stock_still_says_why`: no stock gives no \"invalid setup\" text, and any refusal names \"no stock\".\n- **`scripts/gate.sh quick`** ran the app suites: 1504 passed, 0 failed.\n- **Named:** post_not_judged 4, stock_sim_document 9, setup_carry 9, carried_verify 8, posting 17, probe_op 11.\n- **`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings`:** clean.\n- No golden or snapshot changed. Fork synced at v0.16.0.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nA GUI post of a probe-only job. The note is a post-report string, and the test reads the same `verification_report` the GUI shows.\n\nChangelog: A probe-only program no longer posts with a misleading \"stock sim did not judge: invalid stock simulation setup\" note; the uncut stock is judged (#592)\n\nFixes #592\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
